{"severity":"warning","file":"errors/undeclared_requirement_1.march","start_line":8,"start_col":4,"end_line":8,"end_col":17,"message":"`first` propagates a requirement it doesn't declare.\n\n`List.head` requires  len(_) > 0\nbut first([]) panics — \"List.head: empty list\"\n\nhelp: declare what `first` actually needs —\n        fn first(xs : {List(Int) | len(_) > 0}) : Int\n`forge fix` can apply this.","code":"undeclared_requirement","fix":{"kind":"replace","start_line":7,"start_col":10,"end_line":7,"end_col":26,"text":"(xs : {List(Int) | len(_) > 0})","applicability":"machine-applicable"},"labels":[],"notes":["`List.head_opt` is `List.head` without the requirement: it returns `Option` instead of panicking.\n    match List.head_opt(xs) do\n      Some(v) -> …\n      None -> …\n    end"],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
